aign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Paradise Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.083333,"lo":-77.333333,"d":910,"ds":"Paradise Island is an island in the Bahamas formerly known as Hog Island. The island, with an area of 277 hectares (685 acres) (2.8 km2/1.1 sq mi), is just off the shore of the city of Nassau, which is itself on the northern edge of the island of New Providence. It is best known for the sprawling resort Atlantis, with its extensive water park rides, pools, beach, restaurants, walk-in aquarium, and casinos.","wpu":"Paradise Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Paradise_Island_Lighthouse%2C_Bahamas.jpg/960px-Paradise_Island_Lighthouse%2C_Bahamas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Matthew's Anglican Church, Nassau","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.07422,"lo":-77.32647,"d":1556,"ds":"St. Matthew's Anglican Church is an historic church in Nassau, Bahamas. It has the distinction of having the oldest church building in the Bahamas and potentially the oldest subsisting building in New Providence.","wpu":"St. Matthew's Anglican Church, Nassau","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/St._Matthew%27s_Anglican_Church%2C_Nassau.jpg/960px-St._Matthew%27s_Anglican_Church%2C_Nassau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Raid on Nassau","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.06,"lo":-77.345,"d":2150,"ds":"The Raid on Nassau, on the Bahamian island of New Providence, was a privately raised Franco-Spanish expedition against the English taking place in October 1703, during the War of the Spanish Succession. The Franco-Spanish victory leading to Nassau's brief occupation and then to its destruction.","wpu":"Raid on Nassau","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/NewProvidenceIsland1803_NPIonly.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"French Cloister at Versailles Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.080278,"lo":-77.31,"d":3125,"ds":"French cloister is situated in the northern Bahamas, on Paradise Island. It is from a 14th-century Augustinian monastery, dismantled and imported from Europe by William Randolph Hearst. Purchased while still in pieces from Hearst's estate by Huntington Hartford and reassembled stone by stone here as the centerpiece of the Versailles Gardens on Paradise Island.","wpu":"French Cloister at Versailles Gardens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Bahamas_1988_%28271%29_Paradise_Island_Versailler_Garten_und_Kloster_%2824102471316%29.jpg/960px-Bahamas_1988_%28271%29_Paradise_Island_Versailler_Garten_und_Kloster_%2824102471316%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fort Montagu","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.0736,"lo":-77.3066,"d":3516,"ds":"Fort Montagu is a small fort of four cannon located on the eastern shore of New Providence Island (Nassau) Bahamas. Peter Henry Bruce oversaw the construction of the fort that began in 1741 to defend the British possession from Spanish invaders.","wpu":"Fort Montagu","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Fort_Montagu_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Fort_Montagu_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Baha Mar","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.073333,"lo":-77.397778,"d":5752,"ds":"Baha Mar is a 1,000-acre (400 ha) resort complex on the island of New Providence in The Bahamas. Owned by Hong Kong–based Chow Tai Fook Enterprises, the establishment opened in April 2017.","wpu":"Baha Mar","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Baha_Mar_Resort_located_in_Nassau%2C_Bahamas.jpg/960px-Baha_Mar_Resort_located_in_Nassau%2C_Bahamas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Discovery Island (Bahamas)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.091111,"lo":-77.406667,"d":6748,"ds":"Discovery Island is a small privately owned island off the coast of Nassau. The western portion of the Island is Balmoral Island, a shore excursion for Royal Caribbean cruise lines. The eastern portion is Sandals Island and is owned by the Sandals Royal Bahamian Resort.","wpu":"Discovery Island (Bahamas)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Discovery_Island_beach_%28far_side%29.jpg/960px-Discovery_Island_beach_%28far_side%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cable Beach, Bahamas","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.07789,"lo":-77.41171,"d":7122,"ds":"Cable Beach is a beach, resort destination, and populated place on the northern coast of New Providence Island in the Bahamas west of Nassau. It spans two and a half miles. It is home to Pompey Market.","wpu":"Cable Beach, Bahamas","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Cable_beach.jpg/960px-Cable_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Lake Cunningham (Bahamas)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.060833,"lo":-77.409722,"d":7210,"ds":"Lake Cunningham is a lake on northern New Providence Island in the Bahamas and the second largest on the island after Lake Killarney.","wpu":"Lake Cunningham (Bahamas)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Reflection_-_panoramio_%2857%29.jpg/960px-Reflection_-_panoramio_%2857%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Blue Lagoon Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.098333,"lo":-77.271111,"d":7359,"ds":"Blue Lagoon Island is a private island located 5 km (3.1 mi) from Nassau, Bahamas, and serves as a local tourist attraction.","wpu":"Blue Lagoon Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Blue_Lagoon.JPG/960px-Blue_Lagoon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"New Providence","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":25.03,"lo":-77.405,"d":8440,"ds":"New Providence is the most populous island in the Bahamas. On the eastern side of the island is the national capital city of Nassau; it had a population of 246,329 at the 2010 Census, and a population of 292,522 at the 2022 census. Nearly three quarters of the Bahamas' population lives on New Providence.","wpu":"New Providence","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/New_Providence_in_Bahamas.svg/960px-New_Providence_in_Bahamas.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Nassau ( NASS-aw) is the capital and largest city of the Bahamas. It is on the island of New Providence, which has a population of 296,522, 74.26% of the country's total population. Nassau is commonly defined as a primate city, dwarfing all other towns in the country.","wpu":"Nassau, Bahamas","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Nassau%2C_Bahamas_aerial_view_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Nassau%2C_Bahamas_aerial_view_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}